WEBVTT

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:06.430
Chapter 17

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:06.430
Gifts from the Spirits

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.030
Is something the matter?

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.480
Nothing really.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.350
I heard a strange voice,

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.030
and I was wondering what it was.

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:42.940
I'm sorry.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:47.450
Anyway, what were you singing?

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:52.130
It's an old Darcsen folk song about
 the feeling of missing one's birth place.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:54.090
My father loved this song.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.060
Is that a Darcsen doll?

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:01.800
Yes. It's a gift for the Festival of Spirits.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.790
Eh?! What?! For whom?

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:08.650
Aren't you being silly? Giving gifts during the Festival of Spirits. Are you a kid?

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:10.590
What's so fun about that?

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:13.810
I think it's a good thing to show gratitude towards...

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:17.720
...the people who take care of you regularly, or the people you care about.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:21.720
I-I guess... But who are you...

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.780
Oh, it's for your brother right? It must be for your brother!

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:25.330
No.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:26.820
Then-

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.750
Oh, the moon.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:38.760
It's the same moon whether you see it from Bruhl or Randgriz, isn't it?

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:40.550
Of course!

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:44.830
Right. Sorry for saying something weird.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.650
Man, talk about random. You weirdo.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:52.860
Mulberry Beach?

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:58.780
The goal of this operation is to annihilate the Imperial stronghold stationed there.

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:03.740
To approach the enemy base, we'll have to go through the beach, which doesn't have much cover.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:10.370
Moreover, the enemy has stationed fortified bunkers on the cliffs.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:15.620
It's a disadvantageous situation where we have no cover,

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:18.510
meaning we'll be completely exposed to enemy fire.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:22.900
It seems that the enemy has not made any
move to attack Gallia from that position.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.430
I wonder if there's any meaning in destroying that base now...

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:31.040
General Damon wishes for Squad 7 to lead the attack.

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:33.440
What about the regular army?

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:37.440
They probably want the militia to test the waters first.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.110
I understand.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.910
I can explain this to your squad members myself.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:48.450
No Ma'am, this is my responsibility as the commanding officer.

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:52.420
Sorry.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:00.430
2nd Lieutenant Gunther!

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:02.800
Sighing is an act of imprudence!

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:04.840
W-Well...

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:09.280
2nd Lieutenant Gunther, I delivered the papers for resource replenishment to your room just now.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:10.970
Please look over it.

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:12.180
Oh... Okay.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:14.560
Excuse me.

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:18.590
What's with her?

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:20.100
Was it a fight?

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.550
No...

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.200
Anyway, why are you here today?

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:27.910
Well, I guess it's okay. Take a look at this.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:36.380
Did you know that Borg and General Damon have been meeting each other lately?

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:37.620
No.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:40.550
Did General Damon make any suspicious movements?

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:43.670
Looks like something's already happened.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:45.500
Ah, no.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:49.920
I haven't forgotten about what happened
 at the Randgriz Castle last month.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:53.640
Borg, achievement medals, the general...

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:55.220
It's quite obvious that-

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:56.690
Ellet.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:00.460
I'm hoping this turns out to be a false alarm.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:02.030
Be careful.

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:06.240
Thanks, Ellet.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:20.420
Alicia?

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:23.630
Sorry, but I'm not Alicia.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:25.510
Nah.

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:32.910
You heard about it from Commander Varrot? {Did we use Commander in previous episodes? It sounds fine, but we can change it to Captain too.}

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:33.810
Yeah.

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:39.930
It's one huge mess.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.150
Thanks to that, everyone hates us now.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.030
Now look at this.

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:52.810
Isn't this a confidential military document?

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.830
What's so confidential about it?

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:59.210
They weren't even keeping an eye on it. I'm just borrowing it.

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.120
At the front lines in northern Gallia,

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.430
there was a mysterious flash of blue light.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:05.920
The 5th Company from the regular army suffered casualties.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:09.970
This requires our attention more than something like Mulberry.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:15.770
That's all for the explanation.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:17.520
Any questions?

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:21.560
In other words, we're going to fight during the Festival of Spirits?

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:23.890
We're not supposed to go out on that day.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:27.930
That's right. It's a day we're supposed to spend at home with those important to us.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:30.040
Battles wait for no one.

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:32.260
Please forget about the Festival of Spirits.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:34.580
Sorry.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:36.240
It's all my fault.

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:37.940
Cut it out!

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:41.320
You always apologize incessantly!

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:43.460
Is that something a commander should do?

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:51.980
Yeah. After getting a medal, you've become arrogant.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:55.850
Rosie...

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:58.940
Achieving such a reward even though you're just from the militia,

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:00.850
you've probably become a thorn in someone's side.

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:03.150
Stop saying such things, Rosie!

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:05.700
It's the top brass who wanted to award him.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.610
It's not the commander's fault.

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:10.440
It's because the commander's been too much of a show-off.

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:13.320
That's why we're being targeted for no real reason.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:14.720
Rosie!

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:16.910
The fault lies with General Damon.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:19.460
That's right. The commander's not to blame.

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:21.700
L-Let's fight together!

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:24.240
We won't lose to the Empire or Damon!

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:25.420
Yeah!

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:25.420
That's right!

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:28.570
Come on.

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:31.810
Alicia, you cheer up too. Okay?

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:34.390
I'm not...

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:39.220
You'll get wrinkles if you continue to be angry. Come on, smile!

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:43.890
Rosie.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.610
Thank you very much.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:48.590
What do you mean?

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:51.070
I haven't done anything to deserve your thanks.

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:53.540
Because of your words,

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:56.160
my brother didn't have to take the blame.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.800
You're getting the wrong impression.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:00.870
I'm just saying what I think.

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:04.530
Talk about gross.

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:05.820
Geez.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:09.430
In this squad, I can't even die in peace.

00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:10.920
You won't die!

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:13.880
No one will die. {except you}

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:42.970
Hi Emile!

00:07:42.970 --> 00:07:44.230
What are you doing?

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:47.680
Is this... Squad 7?

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:50.110
It's the Festival of Spirits after all!

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:52.670
You have to give gifts.

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:54.760
A gift?

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:59.010
Why do I have to give Welkin something like that?

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:00.850
But he's the commander...

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:03.180
That has nothing to do with this!

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:04.740
Lovers' quarrel?

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:06.150
No way!

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:07.720
A-Anyway,

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:09.890
I'm tired and busy.

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:12.940
I don't have time for the Festival of Spirits!

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:22.450
I'm such an idiot.

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:24.660
Faldio won't have to worry anymore.

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:27.550
Welkin's an idiot!

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:31.970
It's going to burn again!

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:32.550
Hot!

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:36.340
Alicia!

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:39.410
Alicia!

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:40.600
What's wrong?

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:42.260
Did you burn yourself?

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:43.900
This is bad.

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:45.930
We need to treat this immediately.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:53.830
T-Thanks, Faldio.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:00.280
I overcooked my bread the last time,

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:01.930
and today I burn myself.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:04.620
My bread isn't fit to be called Meister level.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:08.110
You should keep it submerged for a bit longer.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:09.850
I-I'm all right.

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:13.250
I told you before, didn't I? My wounds heal really quickly. {I smell a Valkyria}

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.720
I'm a bit worried about the fire.

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:17.880
I need to take a look.

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:18.680
See you. Thanks!

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:41.990
I'm an idiot.

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:51.710
Isara.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:53.620
What are you doing?

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:55.880
Umm...

00:09:56.930 --> 00:10:00.110
A gift for the Festival of Spirits or something?

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:06.840
Can you keep this a secret?

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.690
Sure. I promise.

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:13.770
What?!

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:17.120
That's why I didn't want to tell anybody about it.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:18.400
Sorry.

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:20.580
Or rather, thanks.

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:22.710
I'm so useless.

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:25.220
I'm lost in my own problems.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:28.110
Are you talking about my brother?

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:34.240
I think I've been too casual with Welkin.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:38.710
I should keep our positions in mind when I interact with him.

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:43.080
Alicia.

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:47.870
What do you think of my brother?

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:49.190
What do I think of him?

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:51.940
Even though I said that just now,

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:53.790
I think that he's a good commander.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:55.650
Is that so?

00:10:56.060 --> 00:10:59.280
The reason my brother seems to perform so well,

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:02.240
is because he tries his best.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:04.450
After losing our father,

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:08.140
he became a bit lost.

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:14.750
Alicia, please don't start to hate my brother.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:20.610
Go ahead! Open it and take a look!

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:21.950
O-Okay.

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:32.820
Quick, take it.

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:34.710
Edy...

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.760
Happy Festival of Spirits.

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:48.270
Same to you, Faldio!

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:49.140
How's your burn?

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:52.530
It has healed completely.

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:53.400
See? {My valkyria blood is awesome, ain't it?!}

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:57.650
Are your parents like this too?

00:11:58.080 --> 00:11:59.240
Who knows?

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:01.860
I grew up in an orphanage.

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:12.370
Isn't this the Ragnite which saved me?

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:15.050
I would like you to accept it again.

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:38.360
Okay.

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:43.610
It's for you. It's the Festival of Spirits, after all.

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:47.440
Sorry! I didn't prepare anything for you.

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:49.330
I-It's all right.

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:54.830
Anyway, have you given your gift?

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:56.540
No, not yet.

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:58.250
I see.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:01.000
Promise me that you'll give it to the person.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.770
I will. Thank you very much.

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:15.270
Brother!

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:17.830
The wind's really strong.

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:20.680
This must be because of the ocean currents.

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:23.660
It should be like this for the whole day.

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:25.380
For the whole day...

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:27.530
What's wrong? Why are you here?

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:30.910
I have something for you.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:34.860
These are...

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:36.590
Smoke bombs.

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:41.570
They're modified to remain in the air for a longer time.

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:46.130
I don't know what the results will be like with that kind of wind, though.

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:49.890
No!

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:54.850
Strong winds seem to blow throughout
 Mulberry Beach for the whole day,

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:59.440
but, in reality, no winds blow for a period of less than an hour during the morning and evening.

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:02.030
We'll attack during those times.

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:04.900
When the smoke bombs are released, everyone will charge in.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:07.820
The Edelweiss will take care of the bunkers.

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:12.350
When we reach the cliffs, we'll attack on foot.

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:15.000
Will things go that smoothly?

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:17.640
I was wondering why you were sneaking around at night.

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:19.750
You were working on something like this, weren't you?

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:20.640
Did you know?

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:22.310
I didn't know either...

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:26.210
Sorry. I didn't tell everyone about it...

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:28.930
because I didn't know if I could complete it or not.

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.730
If you hadn't complete it,

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:33.810
then we would've become sitting ducks, right?

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:37.180
Rosie, don't say such things.

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:40.890
You should be thanking Isara, not saying such sarcastic things.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:57.860
Rosie.

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:08.470
Although the Festival of Spirits is over...

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:11.520
What's the meaning of this?

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:13.950
This is a traditional Darcsen lucky charm.

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:16.050
It can ward off evil.

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:21.480
Why give it to me? Why don't you just give it to your precious brother?

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:25.450
But, you're going to be at the head of the assault, right?

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:30.710
I feel that protecting you, Rosie, 
is the same as protecting all of Squad 7.

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:32.620
Seriously...

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:36.180
You're different from your brother. You have a way with words.

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:00.220
Isara, are you ready?

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:01.780
Yes, brother.

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:04.120
All right. Release the smoke bombs!

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:10.110
All troops, advance!

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:19.850
They're trying to approach us by taking advantage of the smokescreen!

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:24.520
Don't falter! The enemy can't see us!

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:25.830
Yes!

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:32.010
The smokescreen is getting thicker!

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:32.880
Damn!

00:16:39.490 --> 00:16:43.020
Sound! Fire at where the enemy cannon's sounds are coming from!

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:47.080
Our immobility is hindering us!

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:50.000
Send out the soliders! Let them taste our bullets!

00:16:57.150 --> 00:17:00.660
What was that? If you're there, you should tell us at least.

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:06.020
There's an enemy strong point at 1 o'clock! Cover me while I go in!

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:07.540
Okay, got it!

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:35.020
Rosie, are you okay?

00:17:35.020 --> 00:17:35.950
Yeah.

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:41.390
What's that?

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:43.970
If I didn't try to pick that up,

00:17:43.970 --> 00:17:46.390
my head would have been shot to pieces. {into thousands of pieces with candy pouring out!}

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:47.470
Rosie!

00:17:47.470 --> 00:17:48.780
You okay?!

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:52.210
Rosie!

00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:54.450
Are you all right?!

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:57.090
Don't shout into my ears.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:01.460
Everyone, it's just a little bit more.

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:02.260
Come with me!

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:03.770
Understood!

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:06.970
Rosie and Isara will standby here.

00:18:06.970 --> 00:18:08.090
The rest, advance with me!

00:18:08.090 --> 00:18:09.190
Don't kid me!

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:09.750
I'm going too!

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:10.830
Standby here!

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:15.080
Brother.

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:17.650
Be careful.

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:19.590
Yeah.

00:18:19.590 --> 00:18:21.490
All right everyone, let's go!

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:22.780
Follow closely!

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:24.450
Yes!

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:27.880
Don't be afraid! Shoot! Keep shooting!

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:31.670
W-What?

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:32.900
What's happening?

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:34.610
T-This is bad!

00:18:34.610 --> 00:18:37.610
The Gallia army is approaching from the southwest direction too!

00:18:37.610 --> 00:18:39.090
What?

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:44.390
Retreat! Retreat now!

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:04.590
Looks like we succeeded.

00:19:04.590 --> 00:19:06.200
Rosie.

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:08.860
How's your wound?

00:19:09.430 --> 00:19:11.200
It's no big deal.

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:14.960
It's all thanks to this lucky charm.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:31.480
Damn! {frking hell you bitch!}

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:12.610
I'm Eleanor Varrot.

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:15.460
I'm a 1st Lieutenant in the Militia.

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:17.360
Our army has high morals,

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:18.670
extraordinary intelligence,

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:20.300
and overwhelming stamina.

00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:23.910
I believe we're the best in the world.

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:27.620
I'm proud of my subordinates.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:29.560
Next on Valkyria Chronicles,

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:32.610
Chapter 18: August Rain.

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:39.250
Our first and foremost duty is to protect the safety and interests of the people.

00:20:35.160 --> 00:20:40.000
Chapter 18

00:20:35.160 --> 00:20:40.000
August Rain
